dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.deduct.call]/4-5, [temp.inst]/2: deducing os<wchar_t, T> from an
os<char, tr<char>> fails at wchar_t vs char, and nothing requires
os<wchar_t, tr<char>> to be complete.  The front end deduced T = tr<char>
from the other argument, ignored the mismatch of the non-dependent argument
wchar_t, and instantiated the substituted parameter type; sb<wchar_t,
tr<char>>::put is ill-formed and was dropped (bin53).  A non-dependent
built-in type argument of the pattern must now equal A's.  In libc++
<sstream> this dropped basic_streambuf<wchar_t, char_traits<char>>::xsputn /
xsgetn (streambuf:268/276; cpp20_libcxx_header_drops/test_sstream_insert.desc).
g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its WRONG
assertion.
